   "title": "Clamped-part and bolt compliance: cylinder, pressure cone (w = 1 and w = 2), simplified VDI bolt",
   "reference": "Closed-form self-consistency reference. Cylinder (outer diameter D_A = 13 mm = head diameter, so no cone): delta_P = 4 l_K / (pi E (D_A^2 - d_h^2)) = 1.41157e-9 m/N for l_K 20 mm, d_h 9 mm, E 205 GPa. Pressure cone, VDI 2230 closed form delta_P = 2 ln[(d_W + d_h)(d_W + w l_K tan(phi) - d_h) / ((d_W - d_h)(d_W + w l_K tan(phi) + d_h))] / (w pi E d_h tan(phi)) with tan(phi) 0.5: w = 1 6.05958e-10, w = 2 3.95129e-10 m/N (the package integrates the cone slice by slice, a different route to the same quantity). Bolt M8 x 40, l_K 20 (shank 18, free thread 2): delta_S = (0.4 d + l_shank)/(E A_N) + l_thread/(E A_3) + 0.5 d/(E A_3) + 0.4 d/(E A_N) = 3.25924e-9 m/N. tan(phi) from the VDI fit at beta_L = 1, y = 2: 0.362 + 0.032 ln(0.5) + 0.153 ln(2) = 0.44587.",
