  {
   "id": "findley-relaxation-closed-form",
   "kind": "function",
   "title": "Preload against time by Findley creep of the clamped plastic (linear viscoelastic superposition): isothermal, two temperature phases, a daily cycle",
   "reference": "Self-consistency reference from an independent numerical solution, not a published figure and not a measurement. Findley power law, linear in stress: creep compliance J(t) = 1 + beta t^n. The preload relaxes by Boltzmann superposition on a joint of bolt compliance delta_S 1.1e-8 and plastic compliance delta_P 8.4e-8 m/N at fixed total length: delta_S F + delta_P [F + beta_ref integral (xi(t) - xi(tau))^n dF(tau)] = (delta_S + delta_P) F0, with the reduced time xi = integral (beta(T)/beta_ref)^(1/n) dt for temperature. The reference solves this Volterra equation here by backward Euler on a fine grid (steps of at most 0.5 % of the elapsed time and 1 h); the package uses an implicit midpoint stepping with far fewer steps, so the two schemes are independent. F0 1500 N, n 0.2. (a) beta 0.15 for 8760 h: 817.01 N. (b) beta 0.15 for 1000 h then 0.6 to 8760 h: 345.97 N. (c) 365 daily cycles of 1 h at beta 0.6 then 23 h at beta 0.15: 535.47 N. NOTE: an earlier version of this package used time hardening (dF/F = -kappa d(beta t^n)); that over-predicts relaxation by about 19 % for (a) (664 N against 817 N) and far more for hot, long holds, which is why it was replaced.",
   "calls": [
    {
     "fn": "creepRelaxNumbers",
     "metric": "F after 8760 h isothermal",
     "unit": "N",
     "args": [
      {
       "F0": 1500,
       "dS": 1.1e-8,
       "dP": 8.4e-8,
       "n": 0.2,
       "phases": [
        {
         "hours": 8760,
         "beta": 0.15
        }
       ],
       "days": 1
      }
